# ECHO types (`@dxos/echo`).
#
# An ECHO type is a schema piped through `Type.Obj` / `Type.Relation`, or a class extending
# `Type.makeObject`. Both forms carry the typename and version in the piped call's argument, which
# the parser does not read — a snippet shows it, and a JS reasoner could lift it later.

@prefix deus: <https://dxos.org/vocab/deus#>.
@prefix echo: <https://dxos.org/deus/module/@dxos/echo#>.
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>.

{ ?s deus:pipedThrough echo:Type.Obj } => { ?s rdf:type deus:EchoType }.
{ ?s deus:pipedThrough echo:Type.Relation } => { ?s rdf:type deus:EchoRelation }.
{ ?s deus:extends echo:Type.makeObject } => { ?s rdf:type deus:EchoType }.
{ ?s deus:extends echo:Type.makeRelation } => { ?s rdf:type deus:EchoRelation }.
